{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And they complained.</b> It is a binyan nif'al, and so the Targum is binyan nif'al: וְאִתְרַעֲמוּ. And so the way of the term תְּלוּנָה is to turn the expression toward the person — מִתְלוֹנֵן, מִתְרוֹעֵם — and it does not say לוֹנֵן, רוֹעֵם. And so the one speaking Old French will say דקומפ\"לישנ\"ט ש\"י בְּלַעַ\"ז — he turns the expression toward himself by saying ש\"י."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {0 "The la'az דקומפ\"לישנ\"ט is Old French se complaint, 'complains'; ש\"י abbreviates שלו ('himself'), reflecting Rashi's point that the French reflexive turns the verb toward the subject."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:52:34.669619619Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}